────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

On a CRLF file, edit_file now applies a multi-line edit when the old_text was written with plain \n, and the result keeps the file's \r\n endings. Committed as d8b84d41. Build, the full cargo test, clippy with -D warnings, fmt --check, the module-size gate and the neutered-guards check all pass.

Step 0: yoagent 0.25.2's EditFileTool looks for old_text as an exact string and does nothing about line endings. There was no CRLF handling upstream to reuse, so the fix lives in yoyo's wrapper, SmartEditTool.

The fix (in `src/smart_edit.rs`, which is now 1977 lines, under the 2000 cap):
• **The rule:** a new function, `crlf_adapted_edit`, handles one case. If the file doesn't contain `old_text` as written, but does contain it once every bare `\n` becomes \r\n, both old_text and new_text are converted that way before the real tool runs.
• **An exact match always wins.** A \r\n that's already there is never turned into \r\r\n.
• **When it runs:** the file is only read when old_text spans more than one line, and only under the existing 100KB size limit.
• **The error message:** if an edit still fails on a CRLF file, one extra line in the error tells the model the file uses `\r\n` endings. This is meant to stop the wrong guess the morning's test run produced.

Tests: all in the new file src/smart_edit_crlf_tests.rs, all comparing exact bytes, and the end-to-end ones run through yoagent's real edit_file:
• The g.txt case from the morning's run now ends up exactly ALPHA\r\nBETA\r\ngamma\r\n.
• A replacement with more lines than the original gets \r\n on every line.
• Cases that must be left alone are left alone: LF files, single-line edits, old_text already in \r\n, and a mixed file where the LF part matches exactly.
• The extra CRLF line appears in the error for a CRLF file and not for an LF file.

Sabotage check: I forced the function to always return None, in one command run on its own and then restored. Exactly the 5 tests that cover the conversion failed, including the g.txt case; all the leave-alone cases stayed green. Nothing marked NEUTERED was left in the file.

Two things that tripped me up:
• I made three edits to smart_edit.rs in parallel and they overwrote each other, so two were lost and I re-applied them one at a time.
• The orphan-modules check finds modules by file name and ignores #[path]. So the test module is declared as mod smart_edit_crlf_tests;, not the crlf_tests name the plan suggested.

Limits (also written into ARCHITECTURE.md):
• Only `\r\n files are handled. Old Mac files that end lines with \r` alone are not.
• The existing whitespace auto-fix calls the inner tool directly and joins lines with \n. So a whitespace-only mismatch on a CRLF file still falls through to the normal error. I found this by reading the code; no test covers it.
